        "inputType": "binary",
        "binaryPropertyName": "attachment_0",
        "question": "Analyze the attached sales invoice or billing statement image and extract the following information:\n\n1. Sales Invoice Number\n2. Supplier Name\n3. Customer Name\n4. Total Invoice Amount\n5. Currency\n6. PO Number / Purchase Order Number\n\n\nImportant:\n- A \"Sales Invoice\" and \"Billing Statement\" are considered the same type of document for this extraction.\n- Read the information directly from the attached invoice/billing statement image.\n- Do not guess, infer, or invent information.\n- If a field cannot be found or is unclear, return \"N/A\".\n- For the sales invoice number, identify the official invoice number, billing statement number, or equivalent document/reference number printed on the document.\n- For the supplier, identify the company or person that issued the invoice/billing statement.\n- For the customer, identify the company or person being billed.\n- For the total amount, use the final total amount payable on the document, not an individual line-item price or subtotal.\n- For the currency, identify the currency associated with the total invoice amount. Return the currency code when available, such as PHP, USD, EUR, etc.\n- For the PO number, identify the Purchase Order (PO), Purchase Order Number, PO No., Customer PO, or equivalent purchase reference shown on the document.\n- If multiple PO numbers are present, list all of them separated by commas.\n- Preserve the exact invoice number, PO number, supplier name, and customer name as shown on the document.\n- Preserve the currency and amount accurately.\n- Do not include any fields other than those specified below.\n- Return valid JSON only. Do not include markdown, code fences, explanations, or additional text.\n\nReturn the result using ONLY exactly this JSON structure:\n\n{\n  \"sales_invoice_number\": \"Write the sales invoice number\",\n  \"supplier\": \"Write the supplier name\",\n  \"customer\": \"Write the customer name\",\n  \"total_amount\": \"Write the total amount\",\n  \"currency\": \"Write the currency\",\n  \"po_number\": \"Write the purchase order number\"\n\"date of invoice\": \"Write the date of invoice\"\n}",
        "simplify": false,
        "visionOptions": {}
      },
